{"Double-negative bug in enableSqlExpressions() function causes it to always return false regardless of feature flag state, completely blocking SQL expressions even when FlagSqlExpressions is explicitly enabled": 0.9812621474266052, "Documentation misleadingly states SQL expressions can be enabled without clarifying that they are disabled by default for security reasons (CVE-2024-9264), that enabling may re-expose RCE/LFI vulnerability, and that users should understand security implications before enabling": 0.10847461968660355, "SQL expressions rejection test lacks explicit verification of the specific error message 'sql expressions are disabled' to confirm flag-based rejection rather than other validation failures": 0.07645537704229355, "Only one test case exercises the disabled-by-default path - missing separate test cases for: empty query string failure regardless of flag, valid query with flag disabled returning specific error, and valid query with flag enabled succeeding": 0.08641085028648376, "SQL parsing via TablesList is invoked during SQL command construction before the feature flag rejection, leaving the parser exposed even when execution is blocked for security reasons": 0.6453256011009216}